                        <title classid="main title" classname="main title" schemeid="dnet:dataCite_title"
                               schemename="dnet:dataCite_title">Monetary Policy Trade-Offs and Monetary Policy Credibility</title> 
                        <description>&lt;p&gt;This chapter focuses on two key aspects of the monetary policy process: the trade-offs between the three goals that fall into the purview of central banks, price stability, output stabilization, and financial stability; and the role of central bank independence and transparency in enhancing the credibility and the efficacy of monetary policy. The chapter presents the theoretical background for each issue and discusses related empirical studies. The emphasis is on how the specific features of </description> 
